      "settlementKey": "eldravireriverrealm:Or'lythae",
      "description": "Mitch Hearthglass is a Hedge tavern keeper with a hard bark, soft center, and a suspiciously accurate sense for which travelers are about to bring trouble through his door. At the Or'lythae Transit Yard, he keeps food, beds, rumors, and local tempers moving for the Choral Synod, acting as uncle, bartender, quartermaster, and reluctant quest broker. He pretends to care only about the tavern, but everyone knows he would fight the fog itself for his people.",
      "settlementAndAncestryTexture": "Or'lythae is a Village in El'dravire Riverrealm, under Parliamentary Government, with low danger, Farming, Partial forest, Deep forest terrain. Local records favor Altruistic, Lawful, Cooperative, Honorable civic habits; common communities include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Halfling — Stout Halfling, Kender, Kithkin. Hedge reads through the Hedge entry of the race compendium, within Halfling and Smallfolk, marked by Ishtanora. Hedge folk are rustic small beings closely tied to rural landscapes and natural cycles. They are deeply grounded in agricultural life and local tradition. Table cues: +2 Charisma, +1 Wisdom, Natural Burrowers, Spiny Quills; starting tendency Altruistic - Lawful - Cooperative - Honorable.",
      "rumors": [
        "Mitch Hearthglass knows why an ichor ledger changed hands last Ishtaday.",
        "Mitch Hearthglass has a contact in Vaelithorne who will deny everything."
      ],
      "plotHooks": [
